Architecture plan for myClawTeam landing page

Product source
- Product/brand name: myClawTeam, from the implementation issues.
- PRODUCT.md is not present in the current repository tree at setup time; future sessions should prefer PRODUCT.md if it is added.

Project shape
- Use Astro as a static landing page framework with Tailwind integration.
- Keep the app mostly server-rendered/static. Use small client-side scripts only for the mobile menu and contact form validation.
- Expected top-level files after Issue #1: package.json, astro.config.mjs, tailwind.config.mjs, tsconfig.json, src/, public/.

Module and file organization
- src/layouts/BaseLayout.astro
  Shared HTML shell, SEO meta, Open Graph/Twitter meta, favicon links, global page wrapper, and common slots.
- src/pages/index.astro
  Final assembled landing page with section anchors: features, community, contact.
- src/components/Nav.astro
  Sticky navigation, desktop links, CTA, and mobile-menu markup/script.
- src/components/Hero.astro
  First viewport hero with headline, supporting copy, primary/secondary CTAs, and dark gradient treatment.
- src/components/FeatureCard.astro
  Reusable icon/title/description card.
- src/components/FeatureGrid.astro
  Section heading and responsive grid populated from shared feature data.
- src/components/Community.astro
  Discord and X cards with invitation copy and outbound links.
- src/components/ContactForm.astro
  Name/email/message form using configured endpoint with mailto fallback and inline validation states.
- src/components/Footer.astro
  Logo, secondary nav, legal/credits row.
- src/content/site.ts or src/data/site.ts
  Shared constants for site metadata, nav links, CTAs, social links, feature-card content, and contact fallback values.
- src/styles/global.css
  Tailwind directives, base styles, focus states, smooth scrolling, and shared CSS variables if useful.
- public/
  Favicon and static assets.

Shared types
- Define simple TypeScript types near shared data if useful:
  NavLink { label: string; href: string }
  Feature { title: string; description: string; icon: string }
  SocialLink { label: string; href: string; description: string }
- Keep types lightweight; avoid extra runtime validation unless later requirements add dynamic content.

Environment configuration
- Use a public Astro environment variable for the third-party form endpoint, for example PUBLIC_FORM_ENDPOINT.
- Provide .env.example with the endpoint placeholder and optional public contact fallback values if needed.
- The form should degrade gracefully to a mailto fallback when no endpoint is configured.

Dependency order between issues
- Issue #1 initializes Astro, Tailwind, and folder structure.
- Issues #2, #3, and #4 build the shared foundation: design tokens/global styles, layout/SEO, and env configuration.
- Issues #5 and #6 create navigation and mobile behavior.
- Issues #7 through #13 create standalone page sections/components.
- Issue #14 assembles Nav, Hero, Features, Community, Contact, and Footer into src/pages/index.astro.
- Issue #15 performs responsive QA across breakpoints after assembly.
- Issue #16 runs the final build and end-to-end smoke test after responsive fixes.

Key design decisions
- Favor Astro components and shared data modules over hard-coded repeated copy in each section.
- Use Tailwind tokens for the dark background, orange accent, typography, spacing, borders, and focus states so later sections remain visually consistent.
- Keep JavaScript minimal and isolated: one script for nav toggle behavior and one for form validation/submission state.
- Make anchor navigation accessible: semantic landmarks, keyboard-focusable controls, aria-expanded for the mobile menu, and visible focus rings.
- Treat the landing page as static-first, with no backend dependency required for local build success.
- Build verification should include astro build, output inspection, anchor-link smoke checks, and a contact-form validation/submission path check.
